{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 requires implementing a `solve(case)` function that performs grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree.\n\nKey requirements:\n1. Consider deeper nodes before shallower nodes (process deepest first)\n2. Never remove: root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented after removal\n4. Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree from the nodes list\n2. Sort nodes by depth (descending - deeper first), with node ID as tie-breaker\n3. For each node in that order:\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's the root\n   - Skip if its symbol is in required_symbols\n   - Check if removing it would still leave all required symbols represented\n   - Check if it has any retained children (if so, skip)\n   - If all checks pass, remove it (mark as removed)\n4. Return removed_node_ids (in order of removal) and retained_node_ids (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo a node cannot be removed if:\n- It's the root (parent is null)\n- Its symbol is in required_symbols\n- It has children that are retained (not removed)\n\nAnd: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nThis means after marking a node as removed, check if all required symbols still have at least one retained node with that symbol.\n\nLet me think about the order: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" And \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\"\n\nSo we process in order of decreasing depth, with node ID as tie-breaker (alphabetically/lexicographically? or numerically?).\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n- nodes: root(depth=0), n1(depth=1, s1, not removable), n2(depth=1, s2, removable), n3(depth=1, s0, not removable), n4(depth=2, s1, removable, parent=n2), n5(depth=2, s2, not removable, parent=n3), n6(depth=2, s0, removable, parent=n1)\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nSorted by depth desc, then node ID:\n- depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\n- depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth 0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, s1, removable, parent=n2):\n- removable: yes\n- symbol s1 is in required_symbols → cannot remove\n- Skip\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, s2, not removable, parent=n3):\n- removable: no → skip\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, s0, removable, parent=n1):\n- removable: yes\n- symbol s0 not in required_symbols\n- has retained children? n6 has no children → ok\n- If removed, required symbols still represented?\n  - \"root\": root node retained → yes\n  - \"s1\": n1 (s1, retained), n4 (s1, retained) → yes\n- Remove n6 → removed: [n6]\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, s1, not removable):\n- removable: no → skip\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, s2, removable):\n- removable: yes\n- symbol s2 not in required_symbols\n- has retained children? n4 is child of n2, n4 is retained → cannot remove\n- Skip\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, s0, not removable):\n- removable: no → skip\n\nProcess root (depth=0):\n- root → never remove → skip\n\nResult:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: sorted [n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, root]\n\nWait, but n4's parent is n2, so if n2 were to be removed, n4 would need to be removed first. But n4 can't be removed (s1 is required). So n2 can't be removed either.\n\nLet me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node lookup and children map\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track retained/removed status\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    # Sort by depth descending, then node ID ascending (tie-break)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if root (parent is null) - but also covered by removable=false usually\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if symbol is required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if has retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(child in retained for child in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols still represented\n        # Remove nid from retained temporarily\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        \n        # Check all required symbols still present\n        symbols_present = set()\n        for rid in retained:\n            symbols_present.add(node_map[rid][\"symbol\"])\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_present):\n            # Confirm removal\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # Restore\n            retained.add(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nLet me trace through the cases to verify.\n\nCase 0:\n- required_symbols: {root, s1}\n- Sorted: n4(d=2), n5(d=2), n6(d=2), n1(d=1), n2(d=1), n3(d=1), root(d=0)\n\nn4: removable=True, symbol=s1 ∈ required → skip\nn5: removable=False → skip\nn6: removable=True, symbol=s0 ∉ required, no children in retained\n  - Remove tentatively, retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n  - Symbols: root, s1, s2, s0, s1, s2 → {root, s1, s2, s0} ⊇ {root, s1} ✓\n  - Confirm: removal_order=[n6], retained={root,n1,n2,n3,n4,n5}\n\nn1: removable=False → skip\nn2: removable=True, symbol=s2, no required. Children of n2: n4. n4 ∈ retained → has retained children → skip\nn3: removable=False → skip\nroot: removable=False → skip\n\nResult: removed=[n6], retained=sorted[n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,root]\n\nCase 1:\nSame structure, same symbols. Let me check if anything different happens.\n- n4: s1 required → skip\n- n5: not removable → skip  \n- n6: removable, s0, no children. Remove tentatively.\n  - retained after: {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n  - symbols include root and s1 ✓\n  - Remove n6\n- n1: not removable → skip\n- n2: has child n4 retained → skip\n- n3: not removable → skip\n- root: not removable → skip\n\nSame result: removed=[n6], retained=[n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,root]\n\nCase 2:\nSame structure again. Same result.\n\nThe algorithm seems correct. Let me clean it up and encode it as JSON.\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        retained.remove(nid)\n        \n        symbols_present = set(node_map[rid][\"symbol\"] for rid in retained)\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_present):\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            retained.add(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. Now I need to encode it as a JSON string in the implementation field.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    # Process deepest nodes first; use node ID as tie-breaker\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove root\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove: check all required symbols remain represented\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        symbols_present = set(node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"] for rid in retained)\\n\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_present):\\n            removal_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            retained.add(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01c7ltQyN2JmT3qojy8DwFn5","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2394},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2394,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":66,"output_tokens":2779,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2342},"service_tier":"standard"}}